<section id="accuracy" class="sheet">
<div class="col sec">
<div class="numbers-head">
<h2 class="h2 tap">In numbers</h2>
<p class="dim">Measured against AudioRealism's recordings of a late TR-909 on a fine grid of knob settings, the unit it is calibrated to. Method: <a href="#made">How it was made</a>.</p>
<p class="dim small">The clips at the top: with the version 1.0 program ROM, a new instance holds the factory patterns. Every knob at its default, in mono, with no effects: each pattern four times at the default tempo, 120.6 BPM, and the song, track 1, at its stored tempo, 110.3 BPM (TEMPO with TRACK 1). The song runs 65 measures.</p>
</div>

<div class="numbers">
<div class="measure">
<div class="figure">
<div class="big">±28 ¢</div>
<div class="what">tom tuning error</div>
<div class="dim small">At the settings Roland's TR-909 software was measured at; its low tom is 79–120 ¢ flat, its high tom 150–210 ¢ sharp. Over 121 settings, ro-drums-909's median is −4, −6 and −10 ¢ (low, mid, high tom).</div>
</div>
<div class="chart range" aria-hidden="true">
<span class="zero" style={`left: ${at(0, -150, 250)}`}></span>
<span class="label ours" style={`left: ${at(-28, -150, 250)}; top: 0`}>ro-drums-909 −28 to +28 ¢</span>
<span class="span ours" style={`left: ${at(-28, -150, 250)}; width: ${width(-28, 28, -150, 250)}; top: 18px`}></span>
<span class="label" style={`left: ${at(-120, -150, 250)}; top: 32px`}>Roland's software: low tom, high tom</span>
<span class="span" style={`left: ${at(-120, -150, 250)}; width: ${width(-120, -79, -150, 250)}; top: 50px`}></span>
<span class="span" style={`left: ${at(150, -150, 250)}; width: ${width(150, 210, -150, 250)}; top: 50px`}></span>
